course: dictionary
lesson: 5663
title: Lithuanian: from a country
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The ending -ian often tells you where something or someone comes from. Lithuania is a country on the Baltic Sea in north-east Europe. So Lithuanian can mean from Lithuania, or to do with its people.
explain: Read the words around the word to decide its meaning. «The Grand Duchy of Lithuania took most Ukrainian lands in the 14th century; its rulers were Lithuanian». Lithuania is named just before it, so Lithuanian must mean from Lithuania. Swap in your meaning: its rulers were from Lithuania. It still makes sense.
explain: Lithuanian can also name a language or a person. Lithuanian is the language spoken in Lithuania, and a Lithuanian is a person from Lithuania. Look at the other words in the sentence to choose the right meaning: a person, a people, or a language.
fact: Lithuania is a country on the Baltic Sea in north-east Europe.
fact: Its capital city is Vilnius.
fact: Lithuanian is a language spoken in Lithuania, and it belongs to the Indo-European family of languages.
fact: A Lithuanian is a person from Lithuania.
fact: The word «Lithuanian» can describe a thing, a person, or a language, so check the sentence to see which one it means.
exercise: «Its rulers were Lithuanian.» What does Lithuanian mean in this sentence? | *From Lithuania, or to do with its people | A very tall tree | A sport played on ice | Something very far away
exercise: Ella says, «I can speak Lithuanian at home.» What does Lithuanian name here? | The capital city, Vilnius | A coin | *The language spoken in Lithuania | The Baltic Sea
exercise: Find and copy the word that names a country: Vilnius | Baltic | *Lithuania | Ukrainian
test: A Lithuanian is a... | Language spoken in Latvia | Mountain in north-east Europe | *Person from Lithuania | Kind of sea
test: What is the capital of Lithuania? | *Vilnius | Tallinn | Riga | Warsaw
exam: Read «the joint Polish-Lithuanian army». Which two countries are named in this army? | France and Spain | *Poland and Lithuania | Ukraine and Russia | Latvia and Estonia
